In part it says:
  Make your way into the first temple - if the monsters get scared,
  you are in the right place.

That is the most likely case but certainly a simplification of the real
conditions which (if I read priest.c properly) indicates you get
sanctuary (scared monsters) when the following conditions are true:
 o the monster being checked is NOT a minion or a rider (Death, Famine,
or Pestilence)
 o your alignment is better than "Sinned" (-3 or higher)
 o the room is a temple (created as such - with altar & priest)
 o the attending priest is still alive
 o its a shrine (?? appears to check that the room has a coaligned
altar)
 o the priest is coaligned
 o the priest is peaceful

>  Is there any other way to tell?
Mentioned before, but worth a repeat - stand on the altar and use :.
The use of "farlook" (;) returns "aligned altar" when used on the
Astral Plane - not very helpful.
You could check the identity of the @'s in the temple but you MUST be
adjacent to get the full identification of a high priest(ess) on the
Astral plane.

The other method mentioned by Jove (encoded in ROT13) is considered a
"spoiler bug" by the development team (SC343-11). See
  http://www.nethack.org/v343/spoiler.html
for its brief description and the list of other spoiler bugs.

